# Create repositories from the picker

`M-n` should initialize a fresh repository only for the ephemeral plain-session
candidate, then create its session while retaining the picker.

    :bins jj tmux cat sh sed

> [!NOTE]
> 'jj', 'tmux', 'cat', 'sh', and 'sed' are available.

    :copy tests/fixtures/jjconfig.toml .jjconfig.toml (copied)
    :w .config/smth/smth.toml (written)

```toml
[repo]
root = "repos"

[tmux]
setup = ": > .smth-ready"
```

    :t rename-session -t 0 runner (success)
    :t resize-window -t runner:0 -x 120 -y 10 (success)
    :t respawn-pane -k -t runner:0.0 'smth --no-base; cat' (success)
    :pane runner:0.0
    :settle -d 2s (settled)

Type a repository name and wait for the ephemeral candidate to become the
retained selection.

    :k detached
    :snap

```terminal
session: detached
  0/1 | [C-r] repo: none
▌  detached                                                                                                            ┃
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────






```

    :k M-n
    :$ sh -c 'until test -f repos/detached/.smth-ready; do :; done' (exit: 0)
    :settle -d 2s (settled)

The picker should remain open with its query cleared, and the control-mode
client should remain attached to the runner session.

    :snap

```terminal
session:
  2/2 | [C-r] repo: none | [C-x] close, [C-f] flag
▌⬤ runner                                                                                                              ┃
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────






```

    :t display-message -p '#{client_session}' (success)

```
runner
```

The repository should be colocated, use the configured root, and be attached to
its live tmux session.

    :$ sh -c 'test -d repos/detached/.jj && test -d repos/detached/.git' (exit: 0)
    :$ sh -c 'tmux show-options -qv -t "=detached:" @smth.repo | sed "s#$PWD#<ROOT>#g"' (exit: 0)

```stdout
<ROOT>/repos/detached
```

A query that sanitizes to an empty name should use the first available numeric
suffix for both the candidate and the new repository session.

    :k ...
    :snap

```terminal
session: ...
  0/2 | [C-r] repo: none
▌  1                                                                                                                   ┃
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────






```

    :k M-n
    :$ sh -c 'until test -f repos/1/.smth-ready; do :; done' (exit: 0)
    :settle -d 2s (settled)
    :$ sh -c 'test -d repos/1/.jj && test -d repos/1/.git' (exit: 0)
    :$ sh -c 'tmux show-options -qv -t "=1:" @smth.repo | sed "s#$PWD#<ROOT>#g"' (exit: 0)

```stdout
<ROOT>/repos/1
```

With a repository context, `M-n` should create the selected workspace normally
instead of initializing a fresh repository.

    :t respawn-pane -k -t runner:0.0 'smth --base repos/detached; cat' (success)
    :settle -d 2s (settled)
    :k blocked
    :snap "/\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2} \d{2}:\d{2}:\d{1,2}/t" "/(?:@|○|◆)\s+([a-z]{8})/w" "/\b([0-9a-f]{8})\b/h"

```terminal
session: blocked
  0/3 | [C-r] repo: ~/r/detached, [C-o] onto: trunk()
▌  detached/blocked                         ~/r/detached.blocked                                                       ┃
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
@  wwwwwwww (no email set) ttttttttttttttttttt hhhhhhhh
│  (empty) (no description set)
◆  wwwwwwww root() hhhhhhhh



```

    :k M-n
    :$ sh -c 'until test -f repos/detached.blocked/.smth-ready; do :; done' (exit: 0)
    :settle -d 2s (settled)
    :snap

```terminal
session:
  4/4 | [C-r] repo: ~/r/detached, [C-o] onto: trunk() | [C-x] close, [C-f] flag
▌⬤ runner                                                                                                              ┃
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────






```

    :t display-message -p '#{client_session}' (success)

```
runner
```

    :$ sh -c 'test -d repos/detached.blocked/.jj && test ! -e repos/blocked' (exit: 0)
    :$ sh -c 'tmux show-options -qv -t "=detached/blocked:" @smth.repo | sed "s#$PWD#<ROOT>#g"' (exit: 0)

```stdout
<ROOT>/repos/detached.blocked
```

